```cpp
#include <string>
#include <regex>

std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdown) {
    // Use a regex to replace markdown tags with HTML tags
    std::regex regex(R"((\*.*?\*)|(\n(.*?)\n))");
    std::string html;
    std::smatch match;

    // Replace markdown tags with HTML tags
    while (std::regex_search(markdown, match, regex)) {
        html += "<p>" + match[1] + "</p>";
    }

    return html;
}
```

This function uses a regular expression to match markdown tags containing asterisks (`*`) and newlines (`\n`), and replaces them with HTML `<p>` tags. The regular expression matches the asterisks and newlines, capturing the content between them. The `std::regex_search` function is used to search for matches in the input string, and the captured content is replaced with HTML `<p>` tags.

Note that this function does not support all markdown features, such as images, links, or tables. For a more robust implementation, you may want to use a markdown parser library like `cpp-markdown` or `lib-markdown` to parse the markdown text and then convert it to HTML.

